-- The collection element is used only through explicit casts, so no cast target
-- constrains its origin. Its decimal origin defaults to F64, which the final F64
-- cast exposes as an invalid same-type cast (invalid_cast.same_source_and_target).
-- If a cast target wrongly constrained the element, the earlier integer cast would
-- make the final cast a valid conversion and this diagnostic would vanish.
values = {1.5, 2.5}
narrow I32 = cast values.get(0) catch:
    then 0
;
text String = cast values.get(0) catch:
    then ""
;
same_default F64 = cast values.get(0) catch:
    then 0.0
;

[:unreachable]
